    "intro_html":  "Andong jjimdak comes from a market town in Korea and it is the quiet cousin to the spicy chicken stews. No chili paste here. The flavor is dark soy, garlic, and a fair amount of sweetness, with Korean glass noodles (dangmyeon) dropped in at the end to soak up everything left in the pot. Those noodles are the best part and everyone at the table knows it. Each bowl runs 562 calories and \u003cstrong\u003e50 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$1.91 a serving\u003c/strong\u003e.",
